<Publication
    title={frontmatter.title}
    subtitle="Accelerating Architectural Workflows Through Automated Code Compliance"
    coverImage={frontmatter.coverImage}
    coverImageAlt={frontmatter.title}
    date="Aug 2025"
    description=`<p>
            CodeCheck investigates how zoning laws, building codes, and regulatory
            processes shape the relationship between architects, clients, and city
            agencies. As cities grow more interconnected, these regulatory systems
            increasingly influence design workflows, often creating bottlenecks that
            slow down decision-making and introduce costly revisions.
        </p>
        <p>
            To address these challenges, the thesis develops a suite of digital tools
            that streamline communication between design and regulation. At the center
            of this system is CodeCheck, a Grasshopper-based tool that performs
            real-time zoning and code compliance checks directly within the design
            environment. By automating validation, CodeCheck reduces administrative
            setbacks and allows architects to focus on spatial thinking rather than
            manual interpretation of regulations.
        </p>
        <p>
            Building on this foundation, the research introduces mMake, a generative
            design component that produces code-compliant massing models in response to
            site boundary conditions. Together, these tools demonstrate how automation
            can support more context-sensitive, efficient, and accountable design
            processes. Future development aims to expand the platform beyond New York
            City to accommodate a broader range of jurisdictions and regulatory
            frameworks.
        </p>
        <p>
            Ultimately, the thesis argues that compliance is not merely a legal
            requirement—it is a critical part of building better cities. By closing the
            gap between design intent and regulatory constraints, CodeCheck contributes
            to smarter, more transparent, and more sustainable urban development.
        </p>
        <p>
            Access the full paper <a
                href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/19mLUw8BhfABcqKxrbzcsgQJkdEec8bNT/view?usp=sharing"
                target="_blank">here</a
            >.
        </p>`
